+- **Effectiveness of the Judiciary's own operations.** All four sampled cases received an evidence-backed verdict with concrete paths, commits, traces and live observations. Two findings and one inconclusive verdict were recorded rather than treating activity as success. The previous cycle's sampled cases were not re-adjudicated (a later sample is a new cycle). A limitation of this office's own measurement is that `finding`/`inconclusive` verdicts remain assertions with evidence references; the deterministic controller reports them as `unresolved`, which conflates a substantiated adverse finding with genuine absence of information. I describe this weakness; I do not propose or implement a change to the audit algorithm or case rules (Act 15 §2).
